  "@type": "tm:ThingModel",
  "title": "Eastron SDM72D-M Three-Phase Energy Meter",
  "description": "Baseline model for the Eastron SDM72D-M multi-function three-phase four-wire energy meter, read over RS-485 Modbus RTU; it applies to meters that report meter code 0x0084 (132) in holding register 0xFC02. A meter that reports 0x0089 is an SDM72D-M-2, which has its own model. The firmware version is not stated.\n\nRegister map: Eastron SDM72D-M User Manual V1.1 (2019), Part 3 Modbus Protocol, printed pages 13-16. Input registers: Input Registers table, printed pages 13-14, read with function code 04, each value an IEEE 754 32-bit float in two consecutive registers. Holding registers: Holding Registers table, printed page 16, read with function code 03, one 16-bit word each. Addresses here are zero-based: the manual's own example reads phase 1 current, register 30007, at start address 0006.\n\nThe manual says the word order is set automatically to normal or reverse and cannot be configured; this model reads the high word first, which is not confirmed on an SDM72D-M: a catalog maintainer confirmed it on 2026-11-13 on an SDM72D-M-2, whose manual carries the same statement. A request may cover at most 30 parameters (60 registers), and the acquisition groups keep to the address ranges the manual lists. Parameters the manual marks as not valid for the wiring system return zero. Units are SI symbols: the manual's VAr and kVArh are var and kvarh here.\n\nLeft out: the configuration holding registers (system type, pulse width and constant, key parameter authorization, parity and stop bits, Modbus address, password, baud rate, display scroll and backlight times, pulse energy type), the write-only reset command and the serial number, which is instance data.",
